{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/chenglou/pretext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pretext"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is a text measurement and layout library from Cheng Lou. TanStack Virtual still owns scrolling, range calculation, item positioning, and scroll-to behavior; Pretext can own the text-height estimate for rows whose height is mostly determined by wrapped text."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful for chat logs, AI streams, activity feeds, comments, changelogs, notifications, and other text-heavy timelines where DOM measurement creates visible correction work."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to use it"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Pretext when each virtual row's height can be derived from:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text content"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The exact canvas font string used by the rendered text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The available content width"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rendered line-height"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Matching whitespace, word-break, and letter-spacing settings"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not make Pretext responsible for rows whose height depends on images, embeds, block markdown, loaded components, or arbitrary CSS layout. For those rows, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureElement"},{"type":"text","value":", call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resizeItem"},{"type":"text","value":" when the extra content resolves, or split the text-only and non-text portions into separate sizing paths."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @chenglou/pretext","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cache "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prepare()"},{"type":"text","value":" by text and text-style inputs. Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout()"},{"type":"text","value":" for the current width. When the width, font, line-height, or text options change, reset Virtual's measurements so offsets are recalculated from the new estimates."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { clearCache, layout, prepare } from '@chenglou/pretext'\nimport { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual'\n\nconst font = '14px Arial'\nconst lineHeight = 20\nconst preparedCache = new Map<string, ReturnType<typeof prepare>>()\n\nfunction getPrepared(row: { id: string; text: string }) {\n  const key = `${row.id}:${font}:${row.text}`\n  const cached = preparedCache.get(key)\n\n  if (cached) {\n    return cached\n  }\n\n  const prepared = prepare(row.text, font, {\n    whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap',\n    letterSpacing: 0,\n  })\n  preparedCache.set(key, prepared)\n  return prepared\n}\n\nfunction estimateRowHeight(row: { id: string; text: string }, contentWidth: number) {\n  const text = layout(getPrepared(row), contentWidth, lineHeight)\n  const textHeight = Math.max(lineHeight, text.height)\n\n  return textHeight + 24\n}\n\nfunction Messages({ rows }: { rows: Array<{ id: string; text: string }> }) {\n  const parentRef = React.useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)\n  const [width, setWidth] = React.useState(640)\n\n  React.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const element = parentRef.current\n\n    if (!element) {\n      return\n    }\n\n    const update = () => setWidth(element.clientWidth)\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(update)\n\n    update()\n    observer.observe(element)\n\n    return () => observer.disconnect()\n  }, [])\n\n  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n    count: rows.length,\n    getItemKey: (index) => rows[index]!.id,\n    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n    estimateSize: (index) => estimateRowHeight(rows[index]!, width - 32),\n  })\n\n  React.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    virtualizer.measure()\n  }, [virtualizer, width])\n\n  React.useEffect(() => {\n    document.fonts.ready.then(() => {\n      preparedCache.clear()\n      clearCache()\n      virtualizer.measure()\n    })\n  }, [virtualizer])\n\n  return <div ref={parentRef}>{/* render virtual rows */}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"robustness-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Robustness checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Match CSS and Pretext inputs exactly. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"font"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"line-height"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"letter-spacing"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"white-space"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"word-break"},{"type":"text","value":" must agree with the rendered row."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer named fonts. System font aliases can map differently between CSS and canvas, especially on macOS."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for fonts before trusting cached measurements. After "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.fonts.ready"},{"type":"text","value":", clear your prepared-text cache, call Pretext's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clearCache()"},{"type":"text","value":", and call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"virtualizer.measure()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rerun "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout()"},{"type":"text","value":", not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prepare()"},{"type":"text","value":", on resize. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prepare()"},{"type":"text","value":" is the expensive per-text setup; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout()"},{"type":"text","value":" is the cheap width-dependent path."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clamp empty text if your UI renders empty rows as one line. Pretext returns zero height for an empty string."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use one sizing owner per row. Do not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureElement"},{"type":"text","value":" for the same row that you also size with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resizeItem"},{"type":"text","value":" or Pretext estimates unless you deliberately want DOM measurement to override the text estimate."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep a fallback for unsupported runtimes. Pretext currently needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Intl.Segmenter"},{"type":"text","value":" and Canvas 2D text measurement."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resizeItem(index, size)"},{"type":"text","value":" when you know a row's final size outside render, such as after markdown preprocessing, image metadata loading, or a controlled expand/collapse transition."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the React Pretext example for a complete chat-style implementation: "},{"type":"link","href":"./framework/react/examples/pretext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Pretext"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"when-to-use-it","text":"When to use it","level":2},{"id":"install","text":"Install","level":2},{"id":"basic-pattern","text":"Basic pattern","level":2},{"id":"robustness-checklist","text":"Robustness checklist","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n[Pretext](https://github.com/chenglou/pretext) is a text measurement and layout library from Cheng Lou. TanStack Virtual still owns scrolling, range calculation, item positioning, and scroll-to behavior; Pretext can own the text-height estimate for rows whose height is mostly determined by wrapped text.\n\nThis is useful for chat logs, AI streams, activity feeds, comments, changelogs, notifications, and other text-heavy timelines where DOM measurement creates visible correction work.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse Pretext when each virtual row's height can be derived from:\n\n- Text content\n- The exact canvas font string used by the rendered text\n- The available content width\n- The rendered line-height\n- Matching whitespace, word-break, and letter-spacing settings\n\nDo not make Pretext responsible for rows whose height depends on images, embeds, block markdown, loaded components, or arbitrary CSS layout. For those rows, use `measureElement`, call `resizeItem` when the extra content resolves, or split the text-only and non-text portions into separate sizing paths.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\nnpm install @chenglou/pretext\n```\n\n## Basic pattern\n\nCache `prepare()` by text and text-style inputs. Run `layout()` for the current width. When the width, font, line-height, or text options change, reset Virtual's measurements so offsets are recalculated from the new estimates.\n\n```tsx\nimport { clearCache, layout, prepare } from '@chenglou/pretext'\nimport { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual'\n\nconst font = '14px Arial'\nconst lineHeight = 20\nconst preparedCache = new Map<string, ReturnType<typeof prepare>>()\n\nfunction getPrepared(row: { id: string; text: string }) {\n  const key = `${row.id}:${font}:${row.text}`\n  const cached = preparedCache.get(key)\n\n  if (cached) {\n    return cached\n  }\n\n  const prepared = prepare(row.text, font, {\n    whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap',\n    letterSpacing: 0,\n  })\n  preparedCache.set(key, prepared)\n  return prepared\n}\n\nfunction estimateRowHeight(row: { id: string; text: string }, contentWidth: number) {\n  const text = layout(getPrepared(row), contentWidth, lineHeight)\n  const textHeight = Math.max(lineHeight, text.height)\n\n  return textHeight + 24\n}\n\nfunction Messages({ rows }: { rows: Array<{ id: string; text: string }> }) {\n  const parentRef = React.useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)\n  const [width, setWidth] = React.useState(640)\n\n  React.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const element = parentRef.current\n\n    if (!element) {\n      return\n    }\n\n    const update = () => setWidth(element.clientWidth)\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(update)\n\n    update()\n    observer.observe(element)\n\n    return () => observer.disconnect()\n  }, [])\n\n  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n    count: rows.length,\n    getItemKey: (index) => rows[index]!.id,\n    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n    estimateSize: (index) => estimateRowHeight(rows[index]!, width - 32),\n  })\n\n  React.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    virtualizer.measure()\n  }, [virtualizer, width])\n\n  React.useEffect(() => {\n    document.fonts.ready.then(() => {\n      preparedCache.clear()\n      clearCache()\n      virtualizer.measure()\n    })\n  }, [virtualizer])\n\n  return <div ref={parentRef}>{/* render virtual rows */}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Robustness checklist\n\n- Match CSS and Pretext inputs exactly. `font`, `line-height`, `letter-spacing`, `white-space`, and `word-break` must agree with the rendered row.\n- Prefer named fonts. System font aliases can map differently between CSS and canvas, especially on macOS.\n- Wait for fonts before trusting cached measurements. After `document.fonts.ready`, clear your prepared-text cache, call Pretext's `clearCache()`, and call `virtualizer.measure()`.\n- Rerun `layout()`, not `prepare()`, on resize. `prepare()` is the expensive per-text setup; `layout()` is the cheap width-dependent path.\n- Clamp empty text if your UI renders empty rows as one line. Pretext returns zero height for an empty string.\n- Use one sizing owner per row. Do not call `measureElement` for the same row that you also size with `resizeItem` or Pretext estimates unless you deliberately want DOM measurement to override the text estimate.\n- Keep a fallback for unsupported runtimes. Pretext currently needs `Intl.Segmenter` and Canvas 2D text measurement.\n- Use `resizeItem(index, size)` when you know a row's final size outside render, such as after markdown preprocessing, image metadata loading, or a controlled expand/collapse transition.\n\nSee the React Pretext example for a complete chat-style implementation: [React Pretext](./framework/react/examples/pretext).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Text Measurement with Pretext\n---\n\n[Pretext](https://github.com/chenglou/pretext) is a text measurement and layout library from Cheng Lou. TanStack Virtual still owns scrolling, range calculation, item positioning, and scroll-to behavior; Pretext can own the text-height estimate for rows whose height is mostly determined by wrapped text.\n\nThis is useful for chat logs, AI streams, activity feeds, comments, changelogs, notifications, and other text-heavy timelines where DOM measurement creates visible correction work.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse Pretext when each virtual row's height can be derived from:\n\n- Text content\n- The exact canvas font string used by the rendered text\n- The available content width\n- The rendered line-height\n- Matching whitespace, word-break, and letter-spacing settings\n\nDo not make Pretext responsible for rows whose height depends on images, embeds, block markdown, loaded components, or arbitrary CSS layout. For those rows, use `measureElement`, call `resizeItem` when the extra content resolves, or split the text-only and non-text portions into separate sizing paths.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\nnpm install @chenglou/pretext\n```\n\n## Basic pattern\n\nCache `prepare()` by text and text-style inputs. Run `layout()` for the current width. When the width, font, line-height, or text options change, reset Virtual's measurements so offsets are recalculated from the new estimates.\n\n```tsx\nimport { clearCache, layout, prepare } from '@chenglou/pretext'\nimport { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual'\n\nconst font = '14px Arial'\nconst lineHeight = 20\nconst preparedCache = new Map<string, ReturnType<typeof prepare>>()\n\nfunction getPrepared(row: { id: string; text: string }) {\n  const key = `${row.id}:${font}:${row.text}`\n  const cached = preparedCache.get(key)\n\n  if (cached) {\n    return cached\n  }\n\n  const prepared = prepare(row.text, font, {\n    whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap',\n    letterSpacing: 0,\n  })\n  preparedCache.set(key, prepared)\n  return prepared\n}\n\nfunction estimateRowHeight(row: { id: string; text: string }, contentWidth: number) {\n  const text = layout(getPrepared(row), contentWidth, lineHeight)\n  const textHeight = Math.max(lineHeight, text.height)\n\n  return textHeight + 24\n}\n\nfunction Messages({ rows }: { rows: Array<{ id: string; text: string }> }) {\n  const parentRef = React.useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)\n  const [width, setWidth] = React.useState(640)\n\n  React.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const element = parentRef.current\n\n    if (!element) {\n      return\n    }\n\n    const update = () => setWidth(element.clientWidth)\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(update)\n\n    update()\n    observer.observe(element)\n\n    return () => observer.disconnect()\n  }, [])\n\n  const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n    count: rows.length,\n    getItemKey: (index) => rows[index]!.id,\n    getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n    estimateSize: (index) => estimateRowHeight(rows[index]!, width - 32),\n  })\n\n  React.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    virtualizer.measure()\n  }, [virtualizer, width])\n\n  React.useEffect(() => {\n    document.fonts.ready.then(() => {\n      preparedCache.clear()\n      clearCache()\n      virtualizer.measure()\n    })\n  }, [virtualizer])\n\n  return <div ref={parentRef}>{/* render virtual rows */}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Robustness checklist\n\n- Match CSS and Pretext inputs exactly. `font`, `line-height`, `letter-spacing`, `white-space`, and `word-break` must agree with the rendered row.\n- Prefer named fonts. System font aliases can map differently between CSS and canvas, especially on macOS.\n- Wait for fonts before trusting cached measurements. After `document.fonts.ready`, clear your prepared-text cache, call Pretext's `clearCache()`, and call `virtualizer.measure()`.\n- Rerun `layout()`, not `prepare()`, on resize. `prepare()` is the expensive per-text setup; `layout()` is the cheap width-dependent path.\n- Clamp empty text if your UI renders empty rows as one line. Pretext returns zero height for an empty string.\n- Use one sizing owner per row. Do not call `measureElement` for the same row that you also size with `resizeItem` or Pretext estimates unless you deliberately want DOM measurement to override the text estimate.\n- Keep a fallback for unsupported runtimes. Pretext currently needs `Intl.Segmenter` and Canvas 2D text measurement.\n- Use `resizeItem(index, size)` when you know a row's final size outside render, such as after markdown preprocessing, image metadata loading, or a controlled expand/collapse transition.\n\nSee the React Pretext example for a complete chat-style implementation: [React Pretext](./framework/react/examples/pretext).\n"}
